<abstract id="abstract">
<p id="p-0001" num="0000">A wrist-worn oximeter samples red and infrared channels at a rate that increases when an accelerometer detects motion, and rejects samples whose motion vector exceeds a learned threshold, improving SpO<sub>2</sub> accuracy during exercise.</p>
</abstract>
